# Try the identity server and the User module end to end.
# Run the app first (https profile), then send these requests top to bottom.
# Works in Visual Studio, Rider, and VS Code with the REST Client extension.

@host = https://localhost:5001
@email = rider@example.com
@password = Passw0rd!
# Cloudflare Turnstile's dummy token. Locally the server uses Cloudflare's "always passes" test secret,
# so any token is accepted; leave the header out to see the 400. Real apps get a fresh token from the Turnstile widget.
@captcha = XXXX.DUMMY.TOKEN.XXXX

### Health check
GET {{host}}/health

### OpenID Connect discovery document
GET {{host}}/.well-known/openid-configuration

### 1. Register a user (anonymous, needs a CAPTCHA token). Creates the sign-in account (auth.AspNetUsers)
# and the account record (users.Accounts, with the date of birth). The handle and display name go in the core
# profile, not here. People aged 13 and over can join: try a date of birth 12 years ago to see the 400 (error code
# too_young; nothing is created or kept). Try one 15 years ago to see the minor claim in step 2's token.
# @name register
POST {{host}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json
X-Captcha-Token: {{captcha}}
# Sign-up is UK-only. Cloudflare adds this header in the deployed environments; locally it's only used if
# SignUp:TrustCloudflareCountryHeader is true. Try FR to see the 403.
CF-IPCountry: GB

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "dateOfBirth": "1990-06-15"
}

### 2. Sign in as that user (local test client, password grant). Works straight away: there's no selfie at sign-up.
# Under-18s (by date of birth) get "minor": "true" in the token (paste it into jwt.io to see).
# @name userToken
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=bjk-local-user&client_secret=local-user-secret&scope=openid profile email bjk.users&username={{email}}&password={{password}}

### 3. My account: email, status, dates, date of birth
GET {{host}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 4. Download my data (what the identity server holds about me), as a JSON file
GET {{host}}/api/me/data-export
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 4a. My age check, needed only to view sensitive posts: NotChecked, 3 tries left. (Step 2's token has no
# age_verified claim.) For an under-18 by date of birth, underAgeByDateOfBirth is true and nothing is offered.
GET {{host}}/api/users/me/age-check
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 4b. Verify my age with a selfie video (liveness, then the face estimate). With the Development providers any
# file passes as the video and the "estimate" is AgeAssurance:Estimator:Development:Age (30 = pass, 20 = photo ID
# needed, 15 = under 18). In the browser, /Account/CheckAge?returnUrl=... records a real one; the web app sends
# signed-in users there when they tap a sensitive post.
POST {{host}}/api/users/me/age-check/face
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=bjk-boundary

--bjk-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="video"; filename="selfie.webm"
Content-Type: video/webm

< ./appsettings.json
--bjk-boundary--

### 4c. Or with a photo of an ID (after "photo ID needed", or instead of the selfie)
POST {{host}}/api/users/me/age-check/document
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=bjk-boundary

--bjk-boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="id.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./appsettings.json
--bjk-boundary--

### 4d. Sign in again: once passed, the access token carries "age_verified": "true" (paste it into jwt.io to see)
# @name userToken2
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=bjk-local-user&client_secret=local-user-secret&scope=openid profile email bjk.users&username={{email}}&password={{password}}

### 5. Admin token (local test client, client credentials)
# @name adminToken
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=bjk-local-admin&client_secret=local-admin-secret&scope=bjk.users bjk.users.manage

### 6. List all accounts (admin). Add &status=Deactivated to see only deactivated ones.
GET {{host}}/api/users?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 7. Forgot password (anonymous, needs a CAPTCHA token). Always 202.
# Email isn't sent yet: in Development the whole email is written to the app's console. Copy the "Password reset code".
POST {{host}}/api/users/password-reset
Content-Type: application/json
X-Captcha-Token: {{captcha}}

{
  "email": "{{email}}"
}

### 8. Set a new password. Paste the reset code from the console, then sign in again (step 2) with the new password.
POST {{host}}/api/users/password-reset/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "token": "PASTE-TOKEN-FROM-CONSOLE",
  "newPassword": "N3wPassw0rd!"
}

### 9. Deactivate my account (confirm with my password). Signed out everywhere; deleted in 90 days unless I come back.
# Watch users.Accounts (Status, DeletionDueAt), users.Outbox (the event) and badjockeys' [messaging].[bjk-core.user-events].
POST {{host}}/api/users/me/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 10. Signing in now fails with invalid_grant
POST {{host}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=bjk-local-user&client_secret=local-user-secret&scope=bjk.users&username={{email}}&password={{password}}

### 11. Reactivate within the 90 days (anonymous, needs a CAPTCHA token). Then step 2 works again.
POST {{host}}/api/users/reactivate
Content-Type: application/json
X-Captcha-Token: {{captcha}}

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 11a. Admin: see an account's age check (status only, never the video) and reset it so the user takes it again
GET {{host}}/api/admin/users/{{register.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/admin/users/{{register.response.body.$.id}}/age-check/reset
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 12. Admin: deactivate, reactivate, or permanently delete now (skips the 90 days)
POST {{host}}/api/users/{{register.response.body.$.id}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/users/{{register.response.body.$.id}}/reactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken.response.body.$.access_token}}

###
DELETE {{host}}/api/users/{{register.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
